      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n1. **Before overwriting** \u2014 Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state (either its previous content if it existed, or a record that it did not exist) into an in-memory write journal.\n\n2. **Rollback on failure** \u2014 If the agent run fails (due to turn caps, unrecoverable errors, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed and deleting newly created files.\n\n3. **All-or-nothing semantics** \u2014 This approach provides all-or-nothing transaction semantics for writes without needing a database, using the journal itself as a transaction log held in the process\u0027s memory for a single run.\n\n4. **Query agent exception** \u2014 The Query agent never uses the rollback path since it has no write tool; the journal type exists in the shared runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually write.",
